            </profile>
            <profile id="a4ec-c6b3-e793-ba7b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and full plate armour. Has a warhorse if mounted. The warhorse may have cloth barding (+4 pts), or plate barding (+6 pts). Army Battle Standard. If the army is led by the King himself the Oriflamme may be carried as the army's battle standard (+50 pts); it may only be accompanied by a unit of Ordonnance Gendarmes, which is immune to panic; if surrendered to a victorious opponent it is worth 250 Victory points. 0-1. (Armies of Chivalry p.58)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="e083-8b01-d376-e92f" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">3+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024" value="2+ with Cloth barding +1 in hand-to-hand only">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="3d23-d8ab-e34e-ab4a" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="e4a3-53f0-2d50-afca" type="atLeast"/>
