  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="71e9-f616-2e62-74ea" name="French Ordonnance Armies (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>FRENCH ORDONNANCE ARMIES 1445-1503 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.58-59). Keeper of the Oriflamme: if the army is led by the King himself, the Oriflamme may be carried as the battle standard (+50 pts). It may only be accompanied by a unit of Ordonnance Gendarmes; that unit is immune to panic; if surrendered, the banner is worth 250 Victory points; its powers are lost when the Battle Standard Bearer is killed. Chicken: Francs-archers fear any formed troops with a Leadership of 7 or more. Swiss mercenaries (Swiss Pikemen and/or skirmishers) are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[French Ordonnance Armies]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-50%, Infantry 25-75% (artillery from the Infantry allocation), Mercenaries 0-20%. For every Ordonnance Gendarme model there must be one Coustillier model and at least one Ordonnance Longbowman model (not enforced). Mercenaries (documented only): a Swiss mercenary contingent can only comprise Swiss Pikemen and/or skirmishers.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
